extends /specs/products/marlin/page-structure/structure/templates/structure/layout-tmpl.jade
block content


    section.source_section
        h2 Simple Tables

        h3 Simple Table - Basic - No scroll
        p This is a sample of table with no scroll
        .source_example(style='overflow: auto;max-height: 500px;')
            .ux3
                .container
                    .col-md-6
                        .fancyTable
                            p Between April 6, 2009, and Jan 3, 2012, we enrolled 452 patients (225 [50%] in the two chemotherapy-alone groups and 227 [50%] in the two chemotherapy plus bevacizumab groups; figure 1). On March 7, 2014, with 348 deaths, the prespecified 346 deaths had been exceeded. Patients were well matched for GOG performance status, ethnicity, histology, disease status, and in-field pelvic recurrences (table 1). Importantly, 337 (75%) of 452 patients had previously received platinum-based radiosensitising chemotherapy, and this proportion was also evenly distributed between those receiving the two chemotherapy regimens.
                            .inline-table
                                .inline-table__head
                                    span.inline-table__label Table x
                                    span.inline-table__title Health Care Utilization by Case/Control Statusa, first paragraph in caption
                                .inline-table__caption
                                    | The second paragraph onwards should be displayed beneath this in plain text. Patients were well matched for GOG performance status, ethnicity, histology, disease status, and in-field pelvic recurrences (table 1). Importantly, 337 (75%) of 452 patients had previously received platinum-based radiosensitising chemotherapy, and this proportion was also evenly distributed between those receiving the two chemotherapy regimens.
                                include ./templates/samples/basic
                                .inline-table__tail
                                    .inline-table__legend Legend Explanatory text usually displayed below the main body of a Table. It normally explains aspects of how the Table data was gathered and put together.
                                    .inline-table__footnote Footnote Describes footnote(s) relating to information in the table. Should be displayed in plain text after the legend. No functional requirements.
                            p Patients were well matched for GOG performance status, ethnicity, histology, disease status, and in-field pelvic recurrences (table 1). Importantly, 337 (75%) of 452 patients had previously received platinum-based radiosensitising chemotherapy, and this proportion was also evenly distributed between those receiving the two chemotherapy regimens.


